      "message": "I am unfamiliar with the ENUMs, but does this leave a hole?\n\n6.2.1.7 Cable Plug\nThe 1-bit Cable Plug field Shall indicate whether this Message originated from a Cable Plug:\n0b Message originated from a DFP or UFP \u003c\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d what you want to ignore (\"to the cable\")\n1b Message originated from a Cable Plug \u003c\u003d\u003d\u003d shouldn\u0027t we **also** ignore this, unless we\u0027re the ones asking?\n\nIs PD_PLUG_DFP_UFP is the mask for bit 8 (0x0100)? Or is it another value?\n(My apologies for not digging deeper into the code to find the returns manually.)\n\nIt might be more elegant to pass the SOP* role with the \"command\", and call a different function depending.\n(i.e. instead of \"ignoring\" the packet, have two separate functions SOP\u0027_SOFT_RESET and SOP_SOFT_RESET -- and #if-define the SOP\u0027 SOFT_RESET as a NOOP unless we\u0027re a VPD-CT/VPD.)",
